# ComfyUI fork workflow (abk234)

This workspace is a **fork**, not a direct clone of upstream for pushing.

## Remotes (do not change casually)

| Remote | URL | Role |
|---|---|---|
| `origin` | `git@github.com:abk234/ComfyUI.git` | **Our fork** — all pushes go here |
| `upstream` | `https://github.com/Comfy-Org/ComfyUI.git` | **Original** — fetch/merge only |

- `upstream` push URL is disabled (`DISABLED_use_origin_fork_only`). Never push to upstream.
- `master` tracks `origin/master`.

## Sync latest upstream into our fork

```bash
./sync-from-upstream.sh
```

That script: `fetch upstream` → `merge upstream/master` → `push origin` only.

Manual equivalent:

```bash
git fetch upstream
git fetch origin
git merge upstream/master --no-edit
git push origin HEAD
```

Verify: `git rev-list --left-right --count upstream/master...origin/master`  
→ left=`0` means fork has all upstream commits; right=`N` are our fork-only commits.

## What stays on the fork only

- Local helper scripts (`start-comfyui.sh`, `stop-comfyui.sh`, `check-comfyui.sh`, `setup-comfyui.sh`, `sync-from-upstream.sh`)
- Workflow/download tooling, chrome extension, docs under this fork
- Runtime ignored: `comfyui.pid`, `/output/`, `/models/`, venvs

## Birthday-card work (eval)

- Generate via ComfyUI UI when possible (PNG embeds workflow metadata; drag PNG onto canvas to reproduce).
- Human index of favorites: `output/birthday_prompt_image_map.md` + `.json` (gitignored under `/output/`).
- Prefer relation-specific messages + locked visual presentation; one relation at a time when iterating styles.

## When user asks to “push” or “sync”

1. Push → `origin` (fork) only.
2. Sync with original → merge `upstream` into local/`origin`, never push to `upstream`.
3. Keep working in this directory (preserve `models/`, venv, `output/`); do not re-clone unless asked.
